text: >-
  4/12/26, 1:59 PM

  Grok

  Find this court document

  Tyler AND Bates 003996-R2 at timestamp

  @ Thought for 1m 10s

  The reference is to an exhibit in the public criminal case State of Utah v.
  Tyler James

  Robinson, Case No. 251403576 (Fourth Judicial District Court, Provo/Utah
  County, Utah).

  documentcloud.org +1

  This is the high-profile case involving Tyler James Robinson (charged with
  aggravated murder and

  related counts in the September 10, 2025, shooting of Charlie Kirk at Utah
  Valley University).

  "Bates 003996-R2" is a Bates-stamped discovery exhibit (standard numbering
  used by the

  prosecution/Utah County Attorney's Office when producing large volumes of
  materials to the

  defense). It refers to a video recording (likely bodycam, stationhouse
  interview, or surveillance

  footage) of Tyler Robinson's encounter with law enforcement. The video shows
  him being read

  his Miranda rights at approximately 6:25 p.m. MDT on September 11, 2025 (with
  an internal video

  timestamp around 03:36:53 or similar, depending on the exact frame).
  instagram.com +1

  The exhibit has been referenced in recent defense filings and analysis
  (particularly around late

  March 2026) to highlight alleged timeline discrepancies: Robinson was already
  in custody and

  mirandized (and reportedly invoked his right to counsel) hours before the
  official "surrender"

  narrative and a Discord confession message attributed to him.
  Podcaster/investigator Baron

  Coleman has prominently discussed and quoted from it in his coverage.
  timesofindia.indiatimes.com

  Where to access related court documents

  Full discovery exhibits like the raw video (Bates 003996-R2) are not publicly
  posted online

  (they are part of voluminous defense discovery—thousands of files, hundreds of
  hours of

  video/audio—and subject to redactions/court controls). However, the motions
  and filings that

  reference or rely on these exhibits are partially public.

  • Best central collection of redacted/public filings: Andrea Burkhart's
  Substack docket page

  for the case (includes charging documents, affidavits, hearing transcripts,
  media exclusion

  motions, discovery-related motions from March-April 2026, etc.):

  → https://andreaburkhart.substack.com/p/charlie-kirk-legal-documents

  Look for the March 30, 2026 redacted defense motion to exclude still
  photographers/TV

  https://x.com/i/grok?focus=1&conversation=2043428489769193802

  1/3


  4/12/26, 1:59 PM

  Grok

  cameras/microphones and the March 21, 2026 motion to vacate/continue the
  preliminary

  X hearing (these discuss discovery processing and voluminous Bates-numberêd
  material.

  andreaburkhart.substack.com

  • Early charging documents (publicly available PDFs):

  • Information/charging document:

  https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/26098838-tyler-robinson-indictment/(or

  direct from Utah County Attorney site). documentcloud.org

  • Probable cause affidavit (redacted):

  https://static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2025/09/tyler-robinson-

  affidavit-redacted.pdf. static.foxnews.com

  • Redacted hearing transcript (Oct. 24, 2025):

  https://static.foxnews.com/foxnews.com/content/uploads/2025/12/tyler-robinson-

  redacted-hearing-transcript.pdf. static.foxnews.com

  • Utah County Attorney's official case updates page (press releases and some
  filings):

  https://atty.utahcounty.gov/media/ckpr. atty.utahcounty.gov

  The exact motion quoting "Bates 003996-R2 at timestamp [XX:XX]" (with the
  Miranda dialogue)

  appears to be an internal defense filing or exhibit index from the March 2026
  wave of discovery

  disputes (Dkt. ~468 range), which has been discussed/quoted in social media
  and Baron

  Coleman's recent analysis but is not yet fully indexed as a standalone public
  PDF. The Substack

  collection above is the most complete public repository.

  If you have a specific filing date, docket number, or more context from the
  reel/video where you

  saw it, I can narrow it further. Court records like these can also be
  requested directly from the

  Utah County District Court clerk's office.

  8 web pages

  • Explore Miranda rights issues

  • Baron Coleman podcast analysis

  https://x.com/i/grok?focus=1&conversation=2043428489769193802

  2/3


  4/12/26, 1:59 PM

